et X'') \\to (Y \\subset Y')$", "MATH_0021": "$\\NL_{X/Y}$", "MATH_0022": "$\\NL_{X/Y}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-match-thickenings}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{spaces-more-morphisms-lemma-deform}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-deform-module-ringed-topoi}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{equation-to-solve-ringed-topoi}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{spaces-more-morphisms-lemma-first-order-thickening-maps}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{spaces-more-morphisms-lemma-first-order-thickening}", "REF_0007": "\\ref{spaces-more-morphisms-lemma-first-order-thickening-maps}", "REF_0008": "\\ref{lemma-choices-ringed-topoi}", "REF_0009": "\\ref{lemma-huge-diagram-ringed-topoi}", "REF_0010": "\\ref{spaces-more-morphisms-section-netherlander}", "REF_0011": "\\ref{section-deformations-ringed-topoi}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{proof}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{proof}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e4a8e4a5d5a0c9d3d9249accb7bbdc5cf00f9ff48ceb42c5f75f16243eec596a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:33d59f32c5e4531c52d27954c9fd614504ecbfd27ae0019238ae1b096b74aa19", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nWe will apply the material on deformations of ringed topoi\nto the small <ACCENT_0001>tale topoi of the algebraic spaces in the lemma.\nWe may think of <MATH_0001> as a closed subspace of <MATH_0002>\nso that <MATH_0003>\nis a morphism of first order thickenings.\nBy Lemma <REF_0001>\nthis translates into a morphism of thickenings of ringed topoi.\nThen we see from More on Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0002>\n(or from the more general Lemma <REF_0003>)\nthat the ideal sheaf of <MATH_0004> in <MATH_0005> is equal to <MATH_0006>\nand this is in fact equivalent to flatness of <MATH_0007> over <MATH_0008>.\nHence we have a commutative diagram\n<MATH_0009>\nPlease compare with (<REF_0004>).\nObserve that automorphisms <MATH_0010> as in (2)\ngive automorphisms <MATH_0011>\nfitting in the diagram above. Conversely, an automorphism\n<MATH_0012>\nfitting into the diagram of sheaves above is equal to <MATH_0013>\nfor some automorphism <MATH_0014> as in (2)\nby More on Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0005>.\nFinally, by More on Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0006>\nif we find another sheaf of rings <MATH_0015> on <MATH_0016>\nfitting into the diagram\n<MATH_0017>\nthen there exists a first order thickening <MATH_0018>\nwith <MATH_0019> and applying \nMore on Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0007>\nonce more, we obtain a morphism\n<MATH_0020> with all the\ndesired properties.\nThus part (1) follows from\nLemma <REF_0008>\nand part (2) from part (2) of\nLemma <REF_0009>.\n(Note that <MATH_0021> as defined for a morphism of algebraic spaces in\nMore on Morphisms of Spaces, Section\n<REF_0010>\nagrees with <MATH_0022> as used in\nSection <REF_0011>.)\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2b1c6422e41bfe91ea243d33bd1abf18ea890fd8f9acf97ca34110e1fa30f562", "unit_id": "inventory:defos:0D17:proof/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:defos:inventory:defos:0D3P:lemma/0001", "hash": "sha256:354b97ab6fa8987bca4b41009a238b3b256a011ba94b5035a870c761998355d0", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 179960, "byte_start": 179603, "file": "defos.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:8cc38e1d05f37a164b5aa2a9ad837a8c00fc81a317b7b2c58ba74e943b416ce2", "line_end": 4834, "line_start": 4827}, "owner_tag": "0D3P", "parent_tag": "0D15", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "defos", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0D15", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\label{lemma-thickening-space-quasi-coherent}", "MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$DQ_X(\\mathcal{F}) \\to DQ_X(\\mathcal{G})$", "MATH_0003": "$F$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-perfect-section-better-coherator}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{lemma}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{lemma}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d842b790843a74c90bd00be3a28bc9cb71962cdce8313ed2c9df1b16d2a72475", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9c83abd4afdd6ee46d8a1adbf591e685be2b11fb1854c401a307edf99c0d60f2", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nIn the situation above assume that <MATH_0001> is quasi-compact and quasi-separated\nand that <MATH_0002>\n(Derived Categories of Spaces, Section\n<REF_0001>)\nis an isomorphism. Then the functor <MATH_0003> is an equivalence of categories.\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bf0c95421eb4ecb7a5981dc01faefa022603a78a2ea9a21c96a86a1f8593b172", "unit_id": "inventory:defos:0D3P:lemma/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:defos:inventory:defos:0D3P:proof/0001", "hash": "sha256:69e4ec2079863e2a31058d565fca20a663ffcf0ad3f094faa4c65b2b6be2f740", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 180625, "byte_start": 179962, "file": "defos.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:67538242c1a086bf2921ccb740a8103ce2bf40c1c26c67aeaa9d2d9b504000ce", "line_end": 4851, "line_start": 4836}, "owner_tag": "0D3P", "parent_tag": "0D15", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "defos", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0D15", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\NL_{X/B}$", "MATH_0002": "$D_\\QCoh(\\mathcal{O}_X)$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\Ext^i_X(\\NL_{X/B}, \\mathcal{F}) \\longrightarrow\n\\Ext^i_X(\\NL_{X/B}, \\mathcal{G})\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$i$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_X \\oplus \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_X \\oplus \\mathcal{G}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-more-morphisms-lemma-netherlander-quasi-coherent}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-huge-diagram-ringed-topoi}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-choices-ringed-topoi}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{proof}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{proof}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R